From d433ddf4e798c5174742999ca32b02474b429f18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: My Naai <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:29:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Booking requests arrive on their own in the panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The salon portal has had live booking requests since the socket work; the panel
did not, so a request that came in while the Booking requests tab was open sat
unseen until somebody pressed Refresh.

`src/services/liveSocket.js` is the smallest thing that fixes it: one socket per
tab to the API, joining the new `admin` room on connect (the API's `join_admin`,
next to the `salon_` / `user_` rooms it already had). The page listens for
`booking_request_created` and `booking_request_updated` and re-reads the list and
the tiles quietly — a toast names the customer who just asked, because an admin
looking at another tab is the case this exists for. The same two events re-count
the inbox, so the sidebar / phone-topbar bell badge moves on whatever page the
admin is on instead of waiting for its next minute.

The event is a signal, never data: it carries ids and a couple of labels, and
every row on screen still comes from the authenticated list endpoint, so the
panel cannot show a request the database does not have. `socket.io-client` is the
one new dependency (the portal already ships it).
